    pr_ref:  # f0e5
    description: "The supply-chain tier classifier assigns each file to a tier (`first_party`, `internal_dep`, `external_dep`, `derived`). Workspace-package source files at canonical monorepo paths are tagged as external-dependency despite the spec's explicit first-party patterns covering them; first-party symbols from in-tree packages are emitted as external symbols with their path collapsed to a `<external>` placeholder. The mis-tiering concentrates on the project's own internal packages — every workspace-sibling pattern fails the classifier in some way.\n\n### Specific symptoms confirmed on hypergumbo self-analysis\n\n**(1) 144 `hypergumbo_*` modules classified as `internal_dep` (tier 2) with `path='<external>'` and `reason='direct dependency (pyproject.toml)'`; 24 more classified as `external_dep` (tier 3).** Examples in `internal_dep`: `hypergumbo_core` itself, `hypergumbo_core.linkers.airflow_framework_dispatch`, `hypergumbo_core.linkers.build_target`, `hypergumbo_core.linkers.controller_routes`. Examples in `external_dep`: `hypergumbo-core`, `hypergumbo-lang-common`, `hypergumbo-lang-extended1`. Verified counts: `nodes_by_tier = {'external_dep': 1228, 'internal_dep': 480}`; `hypergumbo_in_external=24`, `hypergumbo_in_internal=144`. The tier classifier reads the root `pyproject.toml` dependency list and treats every entry in `[project.dependencies]` as external/internal direct dep; in a workspace/monorepo where sibling packages list each other as dependencies (the normal pattern), this mis-classifies every workspace package as external. Tier asymmetry: `hypergumbo_core` (154 externals), `hypergumbo_lang_common` (40), `hypergumbo_lang_extended1` (56), `hypergumbo_lang_mainstream` (52), `hypergumbo_lang_rust_analyzer` (2) all get `internal_dep` with `reason='direct dependency (pyproject.toml)'`; `hypergumbo_tracker` (27) gets `external_dep` with `reason='unresolved external reference'` — because the root `pyproject.toml` names the lang packages and core but NOT tracker, so tracker falls through to the unresolved-external path.\n\n**(2) 366 `imports` edges target `external_symbol` nodes whose `canonical_name` starts with `python:hypergumbo_` (first-party workspace packages mis-routed as externals).** 331 unique such nodes including `__version__`, `parse_tier_spec`, `fold_array_join`, `scip_pb2.Index`. All have `path='<external>'` and supply_chain tiers `internal_dep` or `external_dep`. The actual function/class definitions exist as separate proper nodes — the import is mis-routed to a phantom external twin instead of being resolved to the real first-party node. 3 of these are orphans (no inbound edges) and correspond to `pyproject.toml [project.scripts]` entries (`hypergumbo_core.cli:main`, `hypergumbo_tracker.cli:main`, `hypergumbo_tracker.cli:textconv_main`); the console-script declaration creates the external node but no edge references it.\n\n**(3) `supply_chain_summary.internal_dep` reports 1 file / 480 symbols with sole path `'<external>'` placeholder; `external_dep` reports 10 files including workspace `pyproject.toml` files plus empty-string and `<external>` paths.** Workspace's own `pyproject.toml` files (`packages/hypergumbo-core/pyproject.toml`, `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/pyproject.toml`, etc.) are tagged `external_dep` instead of `first_party` — they're not recognized as workspace-config files. Internal-dep symbols are routed to the placeholder path `<external>` rather than to their real workspace paths, treating them as out-of-tree.\n\n### Invariant\n\nWorkspace-package source at `packages/*/src/` (or analogous monorepo layout) should be `first_party`. Workspace dependency declarations should be `internal_dep`. First-party symbols should preserve their real path, not collapse to `<external>` placeholder. Workspace `pyproject.toml` files should be recognized as workspace-config (`first_party`), not external. The tier classifier must enumerate `packages/*/pyproject.toml` and treat all workspace members as workspace-internal regardless of how they appear in dependency declarations.\n\n### Scope\n\nAffects every workspace-internal package on the analyzed repository. On hypergumbo self-analysis: 144 + 24 = 168 `hypergumbo_*` modules mis-tiered, 366 `imports` edges mis-routed to phantom externals, 331 unique mis-routed external nodes. Aggregate impact: roughly 22% of Python externals are recoverable as first-party.\n\n### Exposure\n\nBehavior-map per-node `supply_chain.tier_name` field, per-node `path` field, `external_symbol` node set, `imports` edge endpoints, and `supply_chain_summary` aggregations.\n\n### Consequence\n\nTier-weighted views (which up-weight first-party signal and down-weight external) systematically demote in-tree symbols that should be highlighted. Centrality-weighted views, default sketch output (`first_party_priority` deprioritizes hypergumbo's own linker modules), and any consumer using tier as a relevance signal get wrong rankings. Cross-package import joins land on phantom external twins rather than real first-party nodes, breaking analysis that walks import edges to definitions.\n\n### Candidate fixes\n\n- Have the tier classifier enumerate `packages/*/pyproject.toml` and treat every workspace-sibling package as `first_party` (or at minimum `internal_dep`), regardless of whether the root `pyproject.toml` names it.\n- Fix the Python analyzer's import-resolution stage to traverse the workspace-sibling package map and resolve `hypergumbo_*` imports to the real first-party nodes rather than emitting phantom external twins.\n- Recognize workspace `pyproject.toml` files (`packages/*/pyproject.toml`) as workspace-config and tier them as `first_party`.\n- Resolve `[project.scripts]` console-script entries to their in-tree definition nodes (avoid orphan external nodes).\n- Add a property test that asserts every `external_symbol` node's `canonical_name` does NOT start with a workspace-package prefix discoverable from `packages/*/pyproject.toml`.\n\n### Subsumed (do not chase)\n\nThis item subsumes INV-nafav, INV-mosar, INV-konuh — which are deleted or will be deleted shortly and should only be referenced in an emergency."  # f0e5
    fields:  # f0e5
      dogfood_anon_id: "ITEM-30ba2a"  # f0e5
      statement: "Workspace-package source at `packages/*/src/` (or analogous monorepo layout) should be first-party. Workspace dependency declarations should be internal-dependency. First-party symbols should preserve their real path, not collapse to a placeholder."  # f0e5
      root_cause: "The supply-chain tier classifier assigns each file to a tier (first-party, internal-dependency, external-dependency, derived). The classifier mis-tiers files that match documented first-party and internal-dependency patterns: workspace-package source files at canonical monorepo paths are tagged as external-dependency despite the spec's explicit first-party path patterns covering them; first-party symbols from in-tree packages are emitted as external symbols, collapsing their path to a placeholder. The mis-tiering is not random; it concentrates on the project's own internal packages."  # f0e5
